Upstream ships data/webui/device_specific/BUILD_RS232/ with no fnconfig.ini
in it (just .keep and autorun.img), so tools/fujinet/build-fujinet-desktop.sh's
collect_outputs() falls back to the generic distfiles/fnconfig.ini, which is
Atari-flavoured (a host list of Atari community TNFS servers). Add the
per-target default so a new install gets host slot 1 = SD, slot 2 =
APPS.IRATA.ONLINE instead, matching the pattern the other BUILD_<TARGET>
directories (e.g. BUILD_ADAM) already follow.

diff --git a/data/webui/device_specific/BUILD_RS232/fnconfig.ini b/data/webui/device_specific/BUILD_RS232/fnconfig.ini
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/data/webui/device_specific/BUILD_RS232/fnconfig.ini
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+[General]
+devicename=FujiNet
+fnconfig_on_spifs=1
+printer_enabled=0
+
+[Network]
+sntpserver=pool.ntp.org
+
+[Host1]
+type=SD
+name=SD
+
+[Host2]
+type=TNFS
+name=APPS.IRATA.ONLINE
